  "result": "Perfect! All 45 tests pass. Here's what I added:\n\n**New error codes in `src/errors.js`:**\n- `INVOICE_INVALID`: Invoice is malformed or missing required fields\n- `LINE_INVALID`: Line is malformed or missing required fields\n\n**New functions in `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **`lineTotal(line)`** \u2014 Calculates `qty \u00d7 unitPrice`\n   - Returns `ok(total)` with the calculated amount in cents\n   - Returns `fail('LINE_INVALID')` if line is missing qty or unitPrice\n\n2. **`invoiceTotals(invoice)`** \u2014 Calculates totals for an invoice\n   - Sums all line totals using `lineTotal()`\n   - Returns `ok({ subtotal, total })` where both are equal for now\n   - Returns `fail('INVOICE_INVALID')` if invoice is malformed\n   - Returns `fail('LINE_INVALID')` if any line is malformed\n\n**Added 21 new tests** covering:\n- lineTotal calculations (various quantities and prices)\n- lineTotal validation (missing fields, null/undefined inputs)\n- invoiceTotals with single and multiple lines\n- invoiceTotals with real invoices from `createInvoice()`\n- invoiceTotals validation (missing lines, malformed lines)\n- Verification that subtotal and total are currently equal\n\nAll calculations use `roundCents()` to ensure money is always stored as integer cents. \u2713",
